  "originalQuery": "Your company is running a PostgreSQL database on Compute Engine, which requires a high availability setup with synchronous replication for a critical application. You are tasked with designing this setup on Google Cloud. Which of the following should you implement?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Deploy PostgreSQL on Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE) with a StatefulSet configuration and PersistentVolumeClaims to handle synchronous replication.<br/>B. Implement a PostgreSQL database using Cloud Bigtable for storage with a replication policy across multiple regions.<br/>C. Set up PostgreSQL with synchronous replication between two Compute Engine instances in different zones and use a Regional Persistent Disk.<br/>D. Use Google Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL with a failover replica in a different zone and enable automatic failover.",
